    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of $x^2$ in $(x^2+5x+2)(x+1)^4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$33$.\n\nAdd the coefficient products from the three pairs of terms whose powers sum to $2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)^4&=1+4x+6x^2+4x^3+x^4\\end{align*}$$\nThe products contributing to $x^2$ are $x^2(1)$, $5x(4x)$ and $2(6x^2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x^2&=1\\times1+5\\times4+2\\times6\\\\\\text{Coefficient of }x^2&=33\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
